#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tangerine-ask: ask an LLM about the document you're reading in the archive.

A document is everything under one /A/B/C/ path of the collections listed in
`indexes:`. The first question about a document crawls it from the archive
server (over localhost) into a SQLite full-text index. The model then answers
with tools that search and read that one document's pages, citing them as
[p:ID]. Pages are stored once by content hash, so near-identical documents
mostly share storage. When the index passes evict_at x index_max_gb, the
least-asked documents are dropped (they re-index on their next question).

Each user brings their own OpenAI or Anthropic API key, stored encrypted here.
nginx sends only signed-in requests, with the user in X-Tangerine-User.

    tangerine-ask serve
"""
